# Copy to .env and adjust. Every setting is optional unless marked required.

# --- Network
# Address on the host the port is published on. 127.0.0.1 = this machine only.
# Use a LAN or VPN address (for example a Tailscale IP) to share with the team.
BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
# Port on the host.
HOST_PORT=3000
# Public URL people use to reach the app, for example https://audit.example.lan
# Leave empty to accept any host name or IP: the protocol is then taken from X-Forwarded-Proto
# (set by a TLS proxy) and is http when the header is absent.
ORIGIN=
# Behind a reverse proxy, you may name the headers to trust instead:
# PROTOCOL_HEADER=x-forwarded-proto
# HOST_HEADER=x-forwarded-host
# ADDRESS_HEADER=x-forwarded-for
# XFF_DEPTH=1

# --- Image
# Which published image tag to run: main (the default branch, updated on every push), a version
# such as v0.1.0, or latest (the newest version tag, once one exists)
MCP_AUDIT_TAG=main

# --- Storage (inside the container; the Compose file mounts the volume here)
DATA_DIR=/data

# --- First admin (optional). Without these, open /setup and enter the code from the log.
# INITIAL_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com
# INITIAL_ADMIN_PASSWORD=at-least-10-characters
# INITIAL_ADMIN_NAME=Your Name

# --- Sign-in method: password (the default) or passkey. With passkey nobody has a password: people
# --- join by an emailed invitation, sign in with a passkey and get back in with an emailed code.
# --- It needs email (below), ORIGIN as an https address, and on a new instance INITIAL_ADMIN_EMAIL
# --- and INITIAL_ADMIN_NAME (no password): the first admin is invited by email. Turning it on for
# --- an instance with passwords DELETES the stored passwords. See docs/deployment.md, Sign-in method.
# SIGN_IN_METHOD=password

# --- A new instance can set itself up from a profile file at its first start: its name, its first
# --- admin (invited by email), library sources, sign-in method and AI gateway. Mount the file into
# --- the container and name its path here. See docs/deployment.md, An instance set up from a profile.
# TENANT_PROFILE=/config/tenant-profile.yaml

# --- For an instance that someone else runs for you (a tenant): a long random token with which the
# --- operator's overview asks GET /api/operator/status for counts, sizes and dates. No names, titles
# --- or documents are returned, and the token cannot sign in. Without it the endpoint does not exist.
# OPERATOR_TOKEN=

# --- MCP: the agent name recorded on AI writes ("Claude on behalf of <user>")
# MCP_AGENT_NAME=Claude

# --- In-app AI (optional; see docs/deployment.md, In-app AI). Settings, AI in the app overrides these.
# LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://litellm:4000
# LITELLM_API_KEY=
# Provider keys for the optional litellm service in docker-compose.yml, for example:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=sk-choose-a-long-random-key

# --- Outbound email (optional; see docs/deployment.md, Email). Needed for invitations, sign-in codes
# --- and security notices. SMTP_HOST and SMTP_FROM switch it on.
# INSTANCE_NAME=Our audit team
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=
# SMTP_FROM=mcp-audit <audit@example.com>

# --- Backups (see docs/backup.md). At least 12 characters; keep a copy outside the server.
BACKUP_PASSPHRASE=

# --- Time zone for log timestamps and report dates
TZ=Europe/Riga

# --- Testing only. Never set in production.
# Enables the seed command and the test login used by end-to-end tests.
TEST_SEED_ENABLED=false
